{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactorExtensive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactorExtensive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_merge_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_merge_parts","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L95-L130","doc":"**Binding accrues `N(q)^{A-1}` of the discarded normalisation — extensive in\nthe constituent count `A`.** Writing an `A`-constituent system as the\nstrand-merge of `A` parts with strand counts `ns` (each `≥ 1`), the total\nstabilisation factor is the product of the parts' factors times\n`N(q)^{|ns|-1}`:\n\n  `stab(Σ nᵢ) = (∏ stab nᵢ) · N(q)^{A-1}`,   `A = |ns|`.\n\nSo the normalisation that does **not** cancel in a binding difference (bound\nsystem minus its free constituents) is exactly `N(q)^{A-1}` — extensive in the\n**constituent count `A`**, independent of the individual strand counts. This\nis the precise sense in which the discarded Markov normalisation is the volume\nterm `∝ A`: it is the residue of `A-1` strand-merges, one factor of `N(q)`\neach (`markovStabFactor_merge`). **Magnitude still open:** whether\n`(A-1)·log N(q)` (times the electron scale) equals `a_V·(A-1)` is the\nprediction, not proved here — the audit measures the `N = 2` reading `5.4×`\nshort. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_exponent_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_exponent_affine","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Closed form of the accumulated log-exponent.** Over `A` strands the\nstabilisation exponent is `A - 1`, an affine function of `A` with unit slope:\n`exponent(A+1) - exponent(A) = 1` for `A ≥ 1`. This is the arithmetic core of\n\"extensive\" — a constant nonzero increment per strand, versus the `0`\nincrement of an intensive invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_not_intensive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_not_intensive","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L73-L85","doc":"**Extensive, not intensive.** For a nontrivial loop value `N(q) ≠ 1` the\nfactor genuinely depends on strand count: `stab(n+1) ≠ stab(n)` (`n ≥ 1`). An\nintensive isotopy invariant is by definition `n`-independent; the\nstabilisation factor is not, so normalising it away removes exactly this\n`n`-dependent (extensive) piece — the term the corpus has been hunting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_merge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_merge","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L60-L71","doc":"**Merge law (extensivity).** Combining an `m`-strand with an `n`-strand\nsystem multiplies their stabilisation factors and one extra `N(q)`:\n`stab(m)·stab(n)·N(q) = stab(m+n)`. Equivalently the exponents satisfy\n`(m-1)+(n-1)+1 = (m+n)-1`, so `log stab` accumulates `+log N(q)` per merge —\nthe volume-like (extensive) growth that a link-invariant normalisation is\ndesigned to cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor_succ","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L50-L58","doc":"**One constant factor of `N(q)` per added strand.** For `n ≥ 1`,\n`stab(n+1) = stab(n)·N(q)`. The per-strand *ratio* is the constant `N(q)`,\nindependent of `n` — the defining property of an **extensive** accumulation\n(an *intensive* isotopy invariant would have ratio `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovStabFactor.markovStabFactor","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovStabFactorExtensive.lean#L43-L48","doc":"The Jones/HOMFLY **stabilisation factor** on `n` strands: the power\n`N(q)^{n-1}` of the loop value `N(q)` that the Markov moves force in order to\nturn the raw Ocneanu trace into a link invariant. Parameterised by the loop\nvalue `Nq` alone — the extensivity structure below is independent of its exact\nform (`-(q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})`, `[N]_q`, …). ","signatureChunk":0}]}